## Director words — preserved exactly
> I think this needs to live in N3NN.    So do you want to get a workflow pages setup for this?   Then we'll return to our work from the returns yesterday.

> I think this design is good. Having it robust enough so when something is built.  We can ref it's workflow pages, in the right book.  What it does, what it's connected to.  I think workflow is a big part of solving this.  So anytime a model completes its work on a new module or it linked or needs other modules we want to track that.

## Preparation and disposition
- Integrated in 01.001.md: N3NN home, module purpose and relationship declarations,
  links to exact workflow books/pages, and dependency accounting at completion.
- Integrated: distinguish executable requirements from evidence and task context.
- Integrated: compute checks recorded relationships; intelligence identifies and
  assesses meaning. A complete declared list is not proof no dependency was missed.
- Integrated: reverse lookup is derived rather than separately maintained by hand.
- Deferred: machine schema, storage/index format, command names, module identifier
  scheme and integration code. Review 0516's returned checker before choosing these.
- Deferred: final runtime book placement/activation. This is the work-book module
  record, not a new law face or a seated runtime.

